# Shared by BOTH Vercel projects, and that is the trap.
#
# This file is applied at UPLOAD time, before either project narrows to its
# root directory. Listing `tualatin/` here to keep it off chutexc therefore
# stripped it from the tualatinxctf upload as well, and that project deployed
# empty - every path 404, including files that plainly exist. An hour lost to
# it. A path excluded here is excluded from every project in the repo, full
# stop.
#
# So the split is enforced the other way round: tualatin/ ships to both, and
# chutexc's own vercel.json redirects /tualatin/* to / so the page is not
# served on the projections domain. tualatinxctf has root directory tualatin/
# and serves it at its own root.
#
# pull/roster/ is safe to list. Neither site needs it - the page embeds
# everything - and it sits above tualatinxctf's root anyway.
pull/roster/
